(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[16 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [17 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [18 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [19 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [20 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [21 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [22 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [23 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [24 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [26 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [28 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [29 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [30 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [31 23 "// an async generator's awaitable never awaited (async_gen_asend_finalize)"] [32 23 "// a built-in type's tp_finalize, the record's fin (TrackFinalizer, queue 241)"] [35 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [37 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [38 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [39 21 "// the work due at its death"] [40 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [41 2 "// aioTask: a registered asyncio task past the strong list (builtins_asyncio.go's registry, queue 224)"] [43 2 "// owner is the interpreter that tracked it (queue 230): its work runs there, nil for the main one before any thread"] [45 2 "// fin is a built-in type's tp_finalize (workFin; queue 241), given the object: it must hold no reference to it"] [47 2 "// seq is the record's order of making (queue 253): a collection's trash is finalized in it, as CPython's lists"] [48 2 "// keep their objects in the order they were tracked"] [52 1 "// finSeq numbers the records (finMu)."] [55 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [62 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [65 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [66 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [68 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [73 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [74 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [75 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [76 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [82 1 "// finDeletedAt is DELETE_FAST of f's fast local i (not unbound) with the check of the value it deletes. The value is"] [83 1 "// read and cleared here and dropped before anything else runs: no other variable, and no frame of a call goi"] [84 1 "// interprets, keeps it (goi's registers keep a returned call's values: queue 218's REQUEST), so that the collection"] [85 1 "// can find it dead."] [103 1 "// finPeek is the address of the value of name in d, before DELETE_NAME or DELETE_GLOBAL deletes it (0: nothing to"] [104 1 "// check); the deletion's moment is then finDeleted's, as DELETE_FAST's (queue 224: `del g` at a module's level)."] [120 1 "// finAddr is o's address for finDeleted when its holder lets it go (0: nothing to check); queue 293: sys.settrace's and"] [121 1 "// sys.setprofile's previous function, the thread's only reference to it, whose __del__ CPython runs as the call"] [122 1 "// drops it (test_sys_settrace's test_reentrancy: a __del__ that sets the trace function)."] [134 1 "// finDeleted is the check of a deleted object at address a."] [149 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [150 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [151 1 "// finalizers are still, then the drain."] [186 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [196 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [199 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [202 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [207 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [208 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [217 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [236 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [247 1 "// TrackFinalizer is a built-in type's tp_finalize (queue 241): fin(o) runs under the GIL at o's death, once, in"] [248 1 "// __del__'s place in the order (a cycle's too). o is a pointer to a non-empty type with no Go finalizer of its own (a"] [249 1 "// type of another package may be given: pysqlite3's cursor); fin takes o as its argument and must hold no reference"] [250 1 "// to it (the record would keep it alive)."] [267 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [293 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [320 4 "// its interpreter ended: no one to run the work in (queue 230)"] [345 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [358 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [379 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [393 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [404 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [405 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [425 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [426 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [431 33 "// get_warnings_attr imports nothing at shutdown (queue 253)"] [458 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [465 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [466 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [483 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [484 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [485 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [497 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [500 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [501 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [525 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [526 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [543 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [546 59 "// _warnings' own path at shutdown (queue 253)"] [560 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [561 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [562 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [563 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [572 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [573 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [574 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [575 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [576 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [587 1 "// track tracks a generator not finished for its finalization. Its frame's pointer back at it becomes an address: Go"] [588 1 "// never finalizes an object that reaches itself (queue 224: no suspended generator's frame let its generator die, so"] [589 1 "// neither close nor \"never awaited\" ran)."] [599 1 "// generator is f's generator (f.f_generator), nil when none, or when it died first."] [626 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [627 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [628 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [629 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [630 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [631 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [632 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [635 22 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [636 2 "// gcDebugUncollectable is gc.DEBUG_UNCOLLECTABLE (the shutdown's garbage list printed, queue 253)"] [638 33 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [642 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [643 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [644 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [645 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [646 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [647 35 "// gc.garbage"] [648 2 "// gcCollecting: a gc.collect() runs (gc.collecting: faulthandler's \"Garbage-collecting\" line, queue 241)"] [652 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [656 18 "// its record when tracked"] [657 18 "// its slots that hold a node, by address: a slot in the node itself (a FutureIter's) must not hold it"] [658 18 "// in step: the slot is a typed pointer (*Dict, *Cell ...), else an Object"] [659 18 "// the nodes they hold, in step"] [666 1 "// cyLeaves are the objects a collection's graph does not walk (queue 241): the dictionaries of the modules sys.modules"] [667 1 "// holds and the builtins' (held from outside: walking them would walk the whole program), and the frames running on a"] [668 1 "// thread's stack (their slots change under the loop; their Go frames hold them). Set by cyCollect, nil otherwise."] [671 1 "// cySetLeaves computes cyLeaves for this collection."] [715 1 "// cyIsNode is whether o is a node: an object whose references cyTraverse lists (CPython's tp_traverse), not a leaf of"] [716 1 "// this collection (cyLeaves), and able to take a probe's Go finalizer (a list's, a dictionary's or a cell's Go finalizer"] [717 1 "// may be tracemalloc's once it traced: then none of them)."] [730 3 "// a frame a Python object may hold (a traceback's, f_back's, gi_frame's), not running on a thread's stack,"] [731 3 "// not of a generator (the generator's slots fold it in: 222's rule)"] [741 1 "// cyWalkable is a generator whose frame's slots can be hidden (queue 224): suspended, with no pointer from its frame"] [742 1 "// back at it (a generator that reaches itself never has a probe run), and its frame not handed out: what else holds"] [743 1 "// an escaped frame is not in the graph."] [748 1 "// cyAllRefs makes cyTraverse list every object a slot holds, not only nodes (the shutdown's walk, exitRefs: queue 253)."] [753 1 "// cyForced are the dictionaries an exit collection gives as dead (queue 253, pylifecycle.go): seeds of the graph,"] [754 1 "// probed, never held, an edge into one reaching nothing; cyForcedSeeds the same as objects; cyWeakAlive, when set,"] [755 1 "// tells whether a weak reference to the trash is outside it (its callback called)."] [762 1 "// cyVisit is cyTraverse's visitor: a slot of the node, its kind (typed: a pointer of a concrete type, else an Object)"] [763 1 "// and the node it holds."] [766 1 "// cyTraverse is tp_traverse (queue 241; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 241\"): f called with each slot of o (a"] [767 1 "// node) that holds a node. Only slots o owns alone are listed: a backing array shared with another holder would hide"] [768 1 "// that holder's reference. A reference the table does not list (a map's, a closure's, a field of a struct that is no"] [769 1 "// object) stays visible to Go's collector, which only keeps more alive."] [837 20 "// handed out as an object: a node of its own (queue 241)"] [844 31 "// _asyncio's Future or Task: the slots of a task's cycle (queue 224)"] [961 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [1007 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [1008 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [1101 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1102 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1103 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers are still; then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1104 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1124 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1221 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1222 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1223 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1224 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1258 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1269 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1): each probe prints to stderr its nodes held from outside that no other probed node holds,"] [1270 1 "// the roots of what it keeps (queue 241: what to look at when a cycle is not found)."] [1305 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [1314 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [1331 1 "// cyClearWeakRefs clears the weak references to the trash's tracked nodes (handle_weakrefs): their callbacks, in each"] [1332 1 "// list's order, returned to be called once all are cleared (a weak reference is never a node: always \"outside\")."] [1344 24 "// a weak reference in the trash itself: no callback (handle_weakrefs)"] [1356 1 "// cyCollect is gc.collect()'s cycle detection: the trash found, PEP 442's order run over it; the number of trash nodes."] [1373 2 "// the trash in CPython's lists' order (cyOrder, queue 253): the finalizers and callbacks in a fixed order"] [1419 1 "// cySeq is a node's record's order, the untracked last."] [1427 1 "// cyCount is the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu held)."] [1447 1 "// cyFind is the cyclic trash: from the tracked nodes (or, only given, from those nodes alone: the resurrection's"] [1448 1 "// check), the graph, its relevant part probed; every probed node restored but the trash's (they keep no Go finalizer)."] [1471 1 "// cyOrder is the trash in the order CPython's lists would hold it (queue 253): its collector moves what a container"] [1472 1 "// reaches behind the container, so the trash runs from what nothing else in it holds (the dead module dictionaries"] [1473 1 "// first, in sys.modules' order, then by the records' order) through the references in their slots' order, breadth"] [1474 1 "// first; a cycle nothing outside it holds starts at its oldest record. A wrapper is finalized before what it wraps"] [1475 1 "// (an unclosed text file flushes its buffer before its raw file closes)."] [1540 1 "// cySeedGraph builds the graph and its relevant part in a frame of its own, so no object of the walk stays in a live"] [1541 1 "// variable of the probe's caller."] [1582 3 "// a dead module dictionary and all it reaches are probed (queue 253)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[94 28] [114 28] [156 16] [156 27] [161 29] [161 56] [169 29] [219 21] [227 27] [271 21] [318 16] [367 29] [387 51] [399 42] [411 55] [420 24] [430 25] [441 64] [452 92] [460 25] [471 28] [471 55] [473 28] [509 16] [509 27] [532 51] [537 16] [545 25] [607 21] [692 33] [705 19] [705 29] [772 13] [782 13] [787 13] [792 13] [797 13] [802 13] [807 13] [812 13] [817 13] [844 17] [869 26] [942 18] [968 21] [972 23] [985 12] [985 28] [991 18] [1020 22] [1020 39] [1048 32] [1153 52] [1162 27] [1162 54] [1170 27] [1241 28] [1245 28] [1246 30] [1255 22] [1375 34] [1396 41] [1431 30] [1530 22] [1554 33]]} (go/file "finalize.go" :imports [


